* Module 1: Guitar Input Interface & Envelope Follower
* Supply: +/-12V

VCC  VCC 0 DC 12
VEE  VEE 0 DC -12

* Input signal: 200mVpp guitar at 220Hz (test)
VIN  IN 0 SIN(0 0.1 220)

* Hi-Z input: 1M to ground, AC couple 100nF
RIN  IN J1 100k
* actually Hi-Z: input resistor to ground at node after coupling
CIN  IN N1 100n
RHI  N1 0 1MEG

* Buffer stage (TL072 opamp A): non-inverting
* Opamp model: simple ideal VCVS with high gain
Ebuf N2 0 N1 0 1
* (real: TL072, use ideal for sim)

* Preamp variable gain 1-20x: non-inverting amp
* Rg=10k, Rf pot 200k
Rg   N2 Nfb 10k
Rf   Nfb Nout 200k
Epre Nout 0 N2 Nfb 1e5

* Envelope follower: half-wave rectifier
Drect Nout Nrect 1N4148
Rrect Nrect 0 100k
* smoothing cap with diode decay
Cenv Nrect 0 1u
* discharge resistor
Rdecay Nrect 0 100k
* buffer output
Eenv ENV 0 Nrect 0 1

* Decoupling
Cdec1 VCC 0 100n
Cdec2 VEE 0 100n

.model 1N4148 D(Is=2.52n Rs=10 N=1.752 Cjo=4p M=0.4 tt=20n)

.control
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-9 vntol=1e-6 method=gear
tran 10u 200m uic
wrdata /tmp/guitar_input_ef.cir.csv time ENV
print v(ENV)
.endc
.end